---
name: harklight
version: "@SERVER_VERSION@"
description: >-
  Send the person a question, a decision with choices or a notice through
  Harklight, and read their answer, with the harklight-agent command.
  Use this when you need the person's answer or decision and they may be away
  from the terminal.
---

# Harklight

Harklight is an attention-based UI that shows this agent's questions and notices
in the person's attention list (iPhone app or web) and returns their answers.
The person connects this computer with `harklight-agent setup` and uses the
same command to refresh the skill. After setup, the `harklight-agent` command needs no connection options.
If you need to check which Server, account or sender IDs this computer can
use, ask the person to run `harklight-agent setup` with no arguments and share
the status it prints. Connecting a disconnected computer requires their
invitation and approval.

Use a sender ID this computer is granted. The setup default grant `app:agent/`
covers any ID that begins with it, such as `app:agent/claude-code` or
`app:agent/codex`. `--display-name` sets the name the person sees.

**Claude Code:** Run `harklight-agent listen --next --session <session>` as a background Bash command in the originating Claude Code session so Claude can resume that session when the command completes, then rearm it if the returned event is something other than the answer.

**Codex:** If the turn ends before the answer arrives, use `codex exec resume <thread-id>` to reopen the original thread and ask it to read the Harklight answer for its existing Harklight session.
